  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This dog wash, run by the Speed Laverie brand (registered business, SIRET 901 474 130 00076), is located on avenue Jean d'Agrève, in the harbour area of Hyères. A self-service station designed to wash and dry your dog in a few minutes, without going through a traditional grooming salon.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the Speed Laverie website, the station runs self-service 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, on avenue Jean d'Agrève (La Plage area, 83400 Hyères), at €10 for the first 10 minutes, then €2 per additional 2-minute block. Washing and drying take about ten minutes. Speed Laverie's dedicated page places this dog wash "on the Hyères harbour"; the harbour launderette is open from 7am to 9pm (the dog wash does not keep these hours). The website does not say which programmes are offered in Hyères or which payment methods are accepted: check on site.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the area combines a regular launderette with the dog wash — bring change or your card depending on the payment method accepted on the machine.</div>

      <p><small>Sources: speed-laverie.fr (Dog Wash Hyères page and harbour launderette page), read on 06/11/2026.</small></p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Hyères harbour and its beaches are right nearby — so you can combine a swim and a rinse without much of a trip: the <a href="/en/fiche-hyeres-merou">beach between L'Ayguade and Les Salins</a>, the <a href="/en/fiche-balade-giens">Giens peninsula</a>, or the <a href="/en/fiche-camping-mediterranee-hyeres">Camping Méditerranée</a> if you're staying overnight nearby.</p>
